ia worldwide, 7 days — read around the world, so it is KEPT OUT of the Indian total.","change":"Indian-language reads vs the 7 days before. Curves only: '—' for a floor.","stage":"From the 30-day curve: At peak (last day = 30-day high) · Building (last 3 days ≥ 70% of peak and +15% on the 3 before) · Cooling (below 70% of peak and −15%) · Elevated (holding at 3× its 30-day median) · Steady · Faded. Floor only = no curve. No stage word = a death reported in the last 30 days.","zone":"Where the Indian-language reading sits: South = Tamil + Telugu + Kannada + Malayalam editions; Hindi; ≥ 60% = that zone, both ≥ 30% = Both, else '-leaning'. Only with enough reads to split.","agreement":"Signals rising: reading (last day ≥ 1.5 × the median of the 7 before; needs a curve) and Google Trending now (on a scan in the last 7 days). 'quiet' = none.","confidence":"High = clears an edition floor with articles in ≥ 2 Indian editions, or ≥ 300 Indian reads a day · Med = clears a floor or ≥ 100 a day · Low = otherwise. Floors: Hindi 300 a day; any other edition 20% of that edition's leader this week (≥ 50 in 7 days).","editions":"Indian editions with an article on this entity (of 12).","consistent":"The newest dated event on file — calendar, Wikidata release / death, Google trending, a main-page feature or the 60-day high. 'Consistent with', never 'because'.","kept":"Kept: film, series, web series, song, entertainment person, athlete, sports event or team (Wikidata P31 / P106, or the tracker's registry), with an India link. Politics, places, generic pages and deaths of anyone else are dropped. Held back: writers, poets and spiritual figures (a secondary screen or music occupation is not enough), sport topic pages with no dated event (Cricket, FIFA, Olympic Games) and adult-search traps in any script.","days":"Wikimedia days are UTC and publish about a day late."}}